<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBHalfTwo
      Source: StGB consolidated, half two (provenance StGB 180, 180a, 181a, 182, 184a, 184b, 184c, 184e, 184j, 184l, with the 184h definition; German governs)
      One combined carrier for the ten sections of half two plus the sexual-act definition. Each section is a
      SectionScope; identifiers resolve within their SectionScope. The same token (for example Person, Produces,
      Possesses, Exploits, StateTasks) may carry a section-specific surface form: each section's variables are declared in
      that section's own groups, exactly as emitted by the per-section build, and the per-section schemas remain the
      canonical single-section substrates. Objective Tatbestand only; intent (Vorsatz/Absicht) excluded; penalty excluded;
      silent repairs against the German recorded in the Flags annexes of the working document, not here.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Half Two (§180 to §184l)</Subject><Verb>commit</Verb><Article>StGB 180, 180a, 181a, 182, 184a, 184b, 184c, 184e, 184h, 184j, 184l</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBHalfTwo</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

